From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 22:55:30 +0800
Subject: dt-bindings: net: toshiba,tc9564-dwmac: Allow MAC address properties

TC956x Ethernet functions may use a board-provided MAC address, including
one stored in an NVMEM cell.

Allow the standard MAC address properties on the PCI function nodes so
device trees can describe mac-address, local-mac-address, or an NVMEM cell
named "mac-address" without triggering schema warnings.

The binding cannot reference ethernet-controller.yaml wholesale because
the node is a PCI device node, so reference only the relevant common
property definitions.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
(cherry picked from commit a00c7a05a7344cc2eee0088218494caff139ca3f)
[SuperKali: ported from radxa/kernel linux-7.0.11, adapted to the toshiba,tc9564-dwmac binding]
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/toshiba,tc9564-dwmac.yaml | 12 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/toshiba,tc9564-dwmac.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/toshiba,tc9564-dwmac.yaml
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/toshiba,tc9564-dwmac.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/toshiba,tc9564-dwmac.yaml
@@ -58,6 +58,18 @@ properties:
     enum:
       - pci1179,0220 # Toshiba TC9564 (a.k.a. Qualcomm QPS615)
 
+  local-mac-address:
+    $ref: /schemas/net/network-class.yaml#/properties/local-mac-address
+
+  mac-address:
+    $ref: /schemas/net/network-class.yaml#/properties/mac-address
+
+  nvmem-cells:
+    $ref: /schemas/net/ethernet-controller.yaml#/properties/nvmem-cells
+
+  nvmem-cell-names:
+    $ref: /schemas/net/ethernet-controller.yaml#/properties/nvmem-cell-names
+
   gpio:
     type: object
     description: Embedded GPIO controller
-- 
Armbian

